[x] Make chezmoi apply safe on devbox =devbox-apply $Found 2026-10-10 (assistant session 13): a full apply on devbox (immutable personal-os image, headless, CHEZMOI_CONTAINER=1 to skip the paru hook) would delete the shpool user units (dot_config/systemd/exact_user removes unmanaged units), replace .bashrc with one that drops the agent-sandbox env line (. ~/.config/environment.d/50-agent-sandbox.conf) and calls fzf/luarocks/starship which are not installed, and install desktop GUI config and services (hypr, sway, waybar, rclone, otelcol). Fix: a devbox hostname block in .chezmoiignore; shpool units managed or exact_ dropped; command -v guards in .bashrc; obsidian.nvim set up only if ~/Documents/knowledge_base exists. Until then only ~/.config/nvim is applied on devbox (plus an empty knowledge_base dir as a stopgap). Also seen: Windows files (Documents/PowerShell, komorebi.json, data/windows_11_packages.json) are not ignored on Linux. UPDATE 2026-10-13 (Darrion: main is the standard branch, other branches for side work; the devbox is mine to configure): prefer a role value in chezmoi data (desktop default, agent-host here) over a hostname check, so another agent host gets the same profile. Since then: ~/.claude/skills/clearhead and ~/.pi/agent/skills/clearhead are applied here (targeted apply), and .chezmoiexternal.toml clones platform. Also review the 18 systemd units and 9 .local/bin scripts one by one; rclone holds Darrion's remotes, skip it. The branch personal-os-immutable-hooks (b54830b, 1338e50) already restricts the paru hook and rclone jobs on immutable targets: merge or reuse it.$ !2 ^2026-10-10T17:41 %2026-10-13T17:16 #01a126e8-3e55-7a51-8b1f-2a595c129918
[x] Install the Clojure toolchain in the user layer =clojure-toolchain $For rwd on the dev pod (2026-10-18): a JDK, the Clojure CLI, and pinned clojure-lsp, clj-kondo and cljfmt, in ~/.local like the LSP servers. nvim already enables clojure_lsp and cljfmt, but neither is installed. Plus an nvim REPL client once Darrion picks one.$ !1 ^2026-10-18T07:52 %2026-10-18T08:32 #01a14dff-3332-75c2-b75b-44fe320bb3f8
[x] Notify on a failed restic backup run =backup-failure-notice $2026-10-24: restic-backup.timer runs daily on the desktop and nothing reports a failed run; it shows only in systemctl --user --failed. chezmoi itself failed to load on the desktop for an unknown time (a root-owned mkosi cache) with nobody told, so this is a real failure mode. Add OnFailure= to restic-backup.service pointing at a small notify unit (notify-send on the desktop). Test by failing a run on purpose. Done 2026-10-24: b3b3c33; a forced failure (transient notify-test running /bin/false) triggered notify-failure@ and notify-send exited 0 at 13:26:45 PDT. Any other timer opts in with one OnFailure= line.$ !2 ^2026-10-24T20:22 %2026-10-24T20:26 #01a16f94-042b-70d1-afe4-73d8b2487b5a
[x] Set up nzbget's user and config on the desktop =nzbget-failing $2026-10-24: Darrion wants nzbget running. It can't start: no nzbget user exists and the Arch package ships no sysusers file, and the unit reads /var/lib/nzbget/nzbget.conf (dir root-owned 750, from 2025-11). Steps (sudo): useradd --system --home-dir /var/lib/nzbget --shell /usr/bin/nologin nzbget; cp -n /usr/share/nzbget/nzbget.conf /var/lib/nzbget/; chown -R nzbget:nzbget /var/lib/nzbget; systemctl reset-failed nzbget; systemctl start nzbget. Then the facilitator's health check confirms it. Done 2026-10-24 14:55 PDT: nzbget 26.3 active, user nzbget (uid 944), listening on 0.0.0.0:6789; health shows the desktop clean.$ !3 +human ^2026-10-24T20:43 %2026-10-24T21:55 #01a16fa7-328b-7811-b4af-9175d96aeb66
[x] An nvim view to pick a landing, read its review note and record a verdict with a key =verdict-picker $Moved from agent-sandbox on 2026-10-25 (Darrion: the nvim view is for them, so it lives in chezmoi; the CLI stays in agent-sandbox). The view calls the CLI and plain git, never reads \$AGENT_RUNS itself: 'agent-verdict --pending' for the list, 'git notes --ref=review show' for the note, 'agent-verdict <id> --agree|--disagree' to record. pick a workspace from 'agent-verdict --pending', load its refs/notes/review into quickfix (and offer :DiffviewOpen on the landed range), then agree or disagree with a key, calling agent-verdict. One layer at a time: wait for Darrion to use the completion first. Open: where it lives (agent-sandbox share/nvim, or Darrion's nvim config).$ !2 ^2026-10-25T18:08 %2026-10-25T23:50 #01a1743f-a1d4-7b60-b347-c86fd6046286
